    "updated_at": "2017-06-20T02:11:37Z",
    "body": "Ah, okay.\r\n\r\nThe original *ideal scenario* may be throw an exception for it, to programatically get notification.\r\n\r\nIn the current implementation focusing some random non-focusable element will result in\r\nfocusing document.body - so it is not a good idea to break this behavior or assumption.\r\n\r\nOn a second thought, I believe the original intention can be achieved via the following code\r\n\r\n```js\r\nfunction focusWithCheck(element) {\r\n  element.focus();\r\n  return document.activeElement === element;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nOf course, you can do whatever (output warning to console) instead of returning a boolean.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
